1
00:00:42,799 --> 00:00:43,600
As agreed.

2
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:44,759
Two.

3
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:50,799
One moment.

4
00:01:03,627 --> 00:01:04,279
(ID Card)

5
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:04,799
Here.

6
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:13,640
(Ma Na)

7
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,400
(I never meant to hurt you.)

8
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,959
(This money is my only chance)

9
00:01:19,439 --> 00:01:20,719
(to change my life.)

10
00:01:23,239 --> 00:01:24,879
(I'm borrowing this from you.)

11
00:01:25,799 --> 00:01:27,400
(I'll pay you back someday.)

12
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,499
=Ren Yu=

13
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:57,048
(Adapted from Lei Mi's novel Ren Yu)

14
00:03:57,049 --> 00:04:00,000
=Episode 19=

15
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:01,080
I'm going to

16
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,959
ask Director Hu for a search warrant.

17
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,360
Yes.

18
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,240
Tai Wei.

19
00:04:06,599 --> 00:04:07,639
The provincial lab says

20
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,520
Zhou Xijie's DNA

21
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:10,840
doesn't match the killer's.

22
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:12,719
He's not even type A.

23
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,120
Take a look.

24
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:33,320
(Forensic Report: Zhou Xijie, type B.
No match to blood sample 23.)

25
00:05:03,879 --> 00:05:05,160
Stop pretending to sleep.

26
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,759
Eat something. You'll feel better.

27
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,800
I just want some quiet.

28
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:25,360
What's wrong?

29
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,600
Feeling down?

30
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,800
Zhong Cheng told me.

31
00:05:48,319 --> 00:05:50,199
Captain, you know that feeling?

32
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,439
It's like...

33
00:05:55,199 --> 00:05:57,399
Say I'm told to make a pork sandwich.

34
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,438
I make the dough with flour,

35
00:05:59,439 --> 00:06:01,240
and the filling with pork.

36
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,199
Every ingredient is right.

37
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,600
But in the end,

38
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,160
it's not a pork sandwich.

39
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,639
It's a hamburger.

40
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:10,759
What's a hamburger?

41
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:12,240
Well.

42
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,160
That's not the point.

43
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,639
The point is,

44
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,360
I can't figure it out.

45
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,120
Something doesn't add up.

46
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,759
We're making

47
00:06:26,319 --> 00:06:27,199
a pork sandwich.

48
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,519
We're stuck.

49
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:32,680
So what do we do?

50
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:40,360
Step back and look at it.

51
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:41,639
How?

52
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:51,518
Hello?

53
00:06:51,519 --> 00:06:51,919
(Captain Wang)

54
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,360
Go ahead.

55
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:53,319
(We found the bike.)

56
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:54,240
You found it?

57
00:06:54,439 --> 00:06:54,759
(Yeah.)

58
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,719
(And the buyer too.)

59
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,639
(We found them both.)

60
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,679
Address.

61
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,279
(Zhishang Street)

62
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:58,959
Good.

63
00:06:59,839 --> 00:07:00,480
Be right there.

64
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:07,120
Let's go.

65
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,399
Let's step back and look.

66
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,439
You can't leave.

67
00:07:15,079 --> 00:07:16,078
What are you doing?

68
00:07:16,079 --> 00:07:17,480
It's broad daylight! Let go!

69
00:07:17,879 --> 00:07:18,560
Give me back!

70
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,758
Stealing a bike in daylight!

71
00:07:20,759 --> 00:07:22,040
You're the thief!

72
00:07:22,199 --> 00:07:24,480
- Your whole family's thieves!
- Then you are...

73
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,878
Is this your bike?

74
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:26,758
Not mine. Yours?

75
00:07:26,759 --> 00:07:27,758
It's a women's bike.

76
00:07:27,759 --> 00:07:28,838
If I let you go now,

77
00:07:28,839 --> 00:07:29,999
how am I supposed to find you?

78
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,078
Stealing in broad daylight!

79
00:07:31,079 --> 00:07:31,839
Let go!

80
00:07:32,399 --> 00:07:33,239
- I won't!
- Break it up!

81
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,878
- Let go!
- Come on, move along!

82
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,838
You shameless jerk!

83
00:07:35,839 --> 00:07:36,439
Captain Wang!

84
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,199
This is...

85
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:39,040
You're finally here.

86
00:07:39,399 --> 00:07:40,319
This is the bike.

87
00:07:41,079 --> 00:07:41,759
Check it.

88
00:07:42,319 --> 00:07:43,120
(Shanghai FOREVER)
This number

89
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,279
(Receipt: 8/8/1993)
matches

90
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,319
(Bought 1 FOREVER Bicycle)
the receipt.

91
00:07:47,879 --> 00:07:48,758
Where'd it come from?

92
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:49,599
What do you mean?

93
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,040
I bought it with my own money.

94
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:52,078
Where?

95
00:07:52,079 --> 00:07:52,959
Who sold it to you?

96
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,360
(Shanghai FOREVER)
None of your business.

97
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:55,720
Watch your attitude.

98
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,600
We're with the police.

99
00:07:58,279 --> 00:07:59,040
Listen.

100
00:07:59,279 --> 00:08:00,240
It's stolen.

101
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,600
No-No way.

102
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,159
My husband

103
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,800
bought it from a bike shop.

104
00:08:07,001 --> 00:08:08,878
(Payment Receipt)

105
00:08:08,879 --> 00:08:10,319
That was last year.

106
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,360
Who can remember that?

107
00:08:17,199 --> 00:08:18,319
Listen.

108
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,959
This is a murder case.

109
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,279
Think carefully.

110
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,878
You can tell me here,

111
00:08:23,879 --> 00:08:25,160
or back at the station.

112
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:27,160
If you can't explain it,

113
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,759
you're both coming in.

114
00:08:30,399 --> 00:08:31,240
Wait, I...

115
00:08:31,759 --> 00:08:32,558
(Yuanhang Repair)
Go.

116
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,319
- Your fault!
- Wait!

117
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:33,719
Come on.

118
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,201
Wait, wait.

119
00:08:34,202 --> 00:08:34,820
No, no!

120
00:08:35,399 --> 00:08:36,919
A junk collector sold it to me.

121
00:08:37,519 --> 00:08:38,320
Never seen him before.

122
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:41,320
So I took a good look.

123
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:42,519
What did he look like?

124
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:45,879
He was filthy all over,

125
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,960
with a beat-up woven sack.

126
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,600
His hair was really long,

127
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:50,759
and greasy.

128
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,120
He looked pretty young,

129
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:55,279
around thirty.

130
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,480
Besides his appearance,

131
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,159
anything else stand out?

132
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,519
Right, right.

133
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:00,600
Up here.

134
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,039
Something was off.

135
00:09:02,519 --> 00:09:03,360
He seemed

136
00:09:04,279 --> 00:09:05,440
a little slow.

137
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:06,600
He couldn't speak clearly.

138
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,120
I felt sorry for him,

139
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,120
so I gave him five yuan extra.

140
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,240
I paid him 35 yuan.

141
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,080
35?

142
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,639
And you charged me 100!

143
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,240
(Recycling center)

144
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,399
(Junk collectors)

145
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,159
(usually have set territories.)

146
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,360
(They don't go far.)

147
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,559
(They use the same recycling centers.)

148
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,000
(If that's true,)

149
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,398
(the owners there)

150
00:09:30,399 --> 00:09:32,200
(may remember who came to sell.)

151
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:41,879
Na.

152
00:09:45,039 --> 00:09:46,639
I made you red-date tea.

153
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,360
It'll help during the contest.

154
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,678
Don't be late.

155
00:09:51,679 --> 00:09:52,239
I know.

156
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:52,799
Good luck.

157
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:53,759
Thanks.

158
00:09:57,679 --> 00:09:58,120
Come.

159
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,639
Hurry and pack up.

160
00:10:01,159 --> 00:10:02,240
Just for the three of us.

161
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,918
Take everything valuable.

162
00:10:03,919 --> 00:10:05,320
We're flying to Los Angeles tonight.

163
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,559
Los Angeles?

164
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,559
So suddenly?

165
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,080
I just want to leave soon.

166
00:10:10,399 --> 00:10:12,239
Should I call Na back?

167
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,000
She just left.

168
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,240
No, no.

169
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,519
Don't tell her.

170
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:16,919
And don't tell anyone else.

171
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,799
I don't want to distract her.

172
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,960
We'll tell her tonight.

173
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:22,679
Dongchen.

174
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,759
Did something happen?

175
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,719
Nothing's wrong.

176
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,519
What could be wrong?

177
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,159
We're sending her abroad to study.

178
00:10:32,679 --> 00:10:33,480
I wanted to leave soon.

179
00:10:34,399 --> 00:10:35,120
Don't overthink it.

180
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:37,879
Make breakfast. I'm hungry.

181
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:38,960
Nothing's really wrong?

182
00:10:39,159 --> 00:10:40,000
Nothing.

183
00:10:54,799 --> 00:10:56,440
You haven't touched your bun.

184
00:10:56,759 --> 00:10:57,960
The contest is soon.

185
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,678
You need something to eat,

186
00:10:59,679 --> 00:11:00,720
or you'll feel weak.

187
00:11:01,279 --> 00:11:02,440
I can't eat this morning.

188
00:11:04,639 --> 00:11:05,639
You don't look well.

189
00:11:06,919 --> 00:11:08,879
Worried you'll forget your lines?

190
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,360
No.

191
00:11:12,039 --> 00:11:13,559
I only have a few lines.

192
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,399
I've practiced them forever.

193
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,559
I know them by heart.

194
00:11:17,879 --> 00:11:18,840
Eat the bun.

195
00:11:21,039 --> 00:11:21,559
Mom.

196
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,240
About Su Lin...

197
00:11:26,039 --> 00:11:27,399
We've got some leads now.

198
00:11:27,679 --> 00:11:29,720
Things are looking up.

199
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,159
Don't think about it.

200
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,279
Focus on the contest, okay?

201
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:58,720
Take your bag.

202
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:02,519
Vincent.

203
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:07,480
Your ticket.

204
00:12:07,919 --> 00:12:08,679
Hold onto it.

205
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:09,759
Ticket.

206
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,919
We're leaving tonight.

207
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,600
I have something important to do.

208
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:16,440
Wait here for me.

209
00:12:16,679 --> 00:12:17,559
I'll be right back.

210
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,440
Remember?

211
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,439
Wait here

212
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,480
for

213
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:23,799
Xiaolan.

214
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,080
Wait for me.

215
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,639
Look. What's this?

216
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,480
Burn incense. Bathe. Bow.

217
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,678
Worship her.

218
00:13:40,679 --> 00:13:41,559
Disdain.

219
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:42,519
Favor.

220
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,039
Lost.

221
00:13:45,039 --> 00:13:46,960
So gross. So cheesy.

222
00:13:47,279 --> 00:13:48,119
Mr. Zhou wrote this.

223
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:48,839
I printed it.

224
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,879
I'll show it to everyone.

225
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:52,679
Quit being so childish.

226
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,279
Na, don't I deserve some praise?

227
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:59,678
Come on, isn't it funny?

228
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:01,519
You used to love this stuff.

229
00:14:12,154 --> 00:14:13,926
(Chaobei Youth
Recitation Contest Program)

230
00:14:13,927 --> 00:14:16,274
(Burn incense. Bathe. Bow. Worship her.
Disdain. Favor. Lost. Zhou Xijie)

231
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,278
Here.

232
00:14:26,279 --> 00:14:27,159
Take a flyer.

233
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,158
Cheer on The Little Mermaid.

234
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:30,320
Thanks! Thanks!

235
00:14:35,279 --> 00:14:36,639
Here. Go hand these out.

236
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:37,840
Hey.

237
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,119
Cheer for us!

238
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,518
(He's a poet at the Cultural Center.)

239
00:14:40,519 --> 00:14:41,759
(Corny and pretentious.)

240
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:42,878
(He's beyond gross.)

241
00:14:42,879 --> 00:14:44,200
(He's creepy.)

242
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,158
(He's useless.)

243
00:14:45,159 --> 00:14:47,039
(Lives off his wife
at the Cultural Center.)

244
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:13,200
She didn't know where she lived.

245
00:15:14,759 --> 00:15:15,559
Still studying?

246
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:17,679
Too late to cram now, isn't it?

247
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:21,840
I can't focus on anything.

248
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:24,480
Na, I'm getting a soda. Want one?

249
00:15:25,399 --> 00:15:26,080
I brought tea.

250
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,518
Na, your cup is so pretty.

251
00:15:28,519 --> 00:15:29,240
Imported?

252
00:15:29,559 --> 00:15:30,440
No idea!

253
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,439
If you want soda, go get it.

254
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,519
You won't have time later.

255
00:15:49,193 --> 00:15:49,913
It's fine.

256
00:15:51,799 --> 00:15:53,158
Girls, time for makeup.

257
00:15:53,159 --> 00:15:54,120
Everyone, follow me.

258
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:54,952
Go.

259
00:16:10,519 --> 00:16:11,120
Yang Le.

260
00:16:14,799 --> 00:16:16,080
I need to get to makeup,

261
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,679
so I'll be quick.

262
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:21,279
Su Lin may still be alive.

263
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,200
My mom found some clues.

264
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,200
Really?

265
00:16:28,519 --> 00:16:29,519
What are you two doing here?

266
00:16:31,039 --> 00:16:31,519
Ma'am.

267
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:33,519
Everyone's changing and doing makeup.

268
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,199
The show starts any minute.

269
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,320
Why are you still here?

270
00:16:37,279 --> 00:16:37,919
Go do your makeup.

271
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:38,799
Yang Le, come with me.

272
00:16:38,919 --> 00:16:39,679
I've been looking for you.

273
00:16:45,519 --> 00:16:47,158
Think we'll win first prize?

274
00:16:47,159 --> 00:16:47,558
This way.

275
00:16:47,559 --> 00:16:48,600
We have to.

276
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,080
I want the college bonus points.

277
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,799
Use the time to go over your lines.

278
00:17:01,559 --> 00:17:03,199
Respected teachers,

279
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,400
dear students,

280
00:17:04,559 --> 00:17:05,680
welcome.

281
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,440
Great writing gives the soul wings.

282
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,759
Recitation brings words to life.

283
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:17,358
Welcome to

284
00:17:17,359 --> 00:17:20,279
this year's Youth Recitation Contest.

285
00:17:20,519 --> 00:17:22,200
Our first performers are

286
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:25,000
Chaobei No. 2 Middle School's team.

287
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,839
Let's give them a warm welcome.

288
00:17:30,599 --> 00:17:31,239
Potato, potato.

289
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:31,919
Palm, palm.

290
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:32,960
Potato, potato. Back, back.

291
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,078
Vocational students, go get changed.

292
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:35,960
Get ready backstage.

293
00:17:36,079 --> 00:17:36,880
Okay.

294
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:37,919
You're on soon.

295
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:38,922
Let's see some energy!

296
00:17:38,923 --> 00:17:39,413
Go.

297
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:40,999
We've worked so hard for this.

298
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:41,960
This is it.

299
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,759
Don't be nervous.

300
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,079
Are we still missing anyone?

301
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:48,079
If someone's not here, go get them.

302
00:17:50,599 --> 00:17:51,400
Hurry up.

303
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,839
Na, where are you going?

304
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:01,759
What now?

305
00:18:02,359 --> 00:18:03,480
Let's just go over first.

306
00:18:03,599 --> 00:18:05,319
Come on, let's go.

307
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,720
Next up, the recitation team

308
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,720
from today's host school,
Chaobei Vocational High School.

309
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,400
- Mr. Zhou.
- (Their piece...)

310
00:18:16,799 --> 00:18:17,720
- Have you seen Ma Na?
- (is...)

311
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,719
(The Little Mermaid.)

312
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:19,440
She's onstage.

313
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,079
She's not.

314
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,519
I've looked everywhere.

315
00:18:23,119 --> 00:18:24,318
(The story of the sea princess.)

316
00:18:24,319 --> 00:18:25,079
Then go find her!

317
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,359
Okay, I'll keep looking.

318
00:18:26,559 --> 00:18:28,239
Please tell Principal Dong.

319
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:28,959
(Unlike the heroines)

320
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,399
(of other fairy tales,)

321
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,358
(she isn't as fortunate.)

322
00:18:31,359 --> 00:18:33,759
(In children's literature,)

323
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,640
(she is a tragic figure,)

324
00:18:36,039 --> 00:18:37,959
(a vivid and striking)

325
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:41,160
(character created by Andersen.)

326
00:18:41,799 --> 00:18:43,558
(Love flows to everyone.)

327
00:18:43,559 --> 00:18:44,639
Ma Na's missing.

328
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,639
(Everyone)

329
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,038
- Where?
- (...finds their way.)

330
00:18:47,039 --> 00:18:47,639
They're looking.

331
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,439
(And the Little Mermaid's...)

332
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,279
- Find her!
- (path...)

333
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:50,518
(leads wherever...)

334
00:18:50,519 --> 00:18:52,920
(she can go.)

335
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:53,559
Good.

336
00:18:53,759 --> 00:18:55,839
Now, please enjoy

337
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,200
The Little Mermaid.

338
00:19:24,039 --> 00:19:24,679
She's back!

339
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,239
Sure it's her?

340
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,160
Yes, it's her!

341
00:19:26,279 --> 00:19:27,319
The show's starting. Later.

342
00:19:28,119 --> 00:19:30,599
Far out in the ocean,

343
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:33,679
the water is as blue

344
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,759
as the prettiest cornflower,

345
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,879
and as clear

346
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:38,960
as crystal.

347
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:42,319
It is very, very deep,

348
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:48,160
so deep, indeed,
that no cable could fathom it.

349
00:19:48,839 --> 00:19:50,880
Many church steeples,

350
00:19:51,559 --> 00:19:54,200
piled one upon another,

351
00:19:54,799 --> 00:20:01,319
would not reach from the ground beneath
to the surface of the water above.

352
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,399
There dwell the Sea King

353
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,160
and his subjects.

354
00:20:07,559 --> 00:20:10,799
The Sea King had
six beautiful daughters.

355
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,358
And the youngest

356
00:20:12,359 --> 00:20:14,839
was the prettiest of them all.

357
00:20:15,279 --> 00:20:19,558
Her skin is as clear and delicate

358
00:20:19,559 --> 00:20:21,759
as a rose-leaf.

359
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:28,919
Her eyes are as blue,

360
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:31,240
as the deepest sea.

361
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:37,799
Nothing gave her so much pleasure

362
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:41,799
as to hear about
the world above the sea.

363
00:20:57,759 --> 00:20:58,799
Because

364
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:03,400
she could not go near
to all those wonderful things.

365
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:08,559
She longed for them more than ever.

366
00:21:10,319 --> 00:21:11,359
Anyone?

367
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:19,960
Anyone here?

368
00:21:21,799 --> 00:21:24,079
Oh, were I but fifteen years old!

369
00:21:24,319 --> 00:21:27,839
I know that I shall
love the world up there

370
00:21:29,039 --> 00:21:32,240
and all the people who live in it.

371
00:21:34,839 --> 00:21:35,559
At last,

372
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:38,319
she reached her fifteenth year.

373
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:42,519
Su Lin.

374
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:48,480
This was the last evening

375
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:52,039
that she could breathe
the same air with him

376
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,480
or gaze

377
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,440
at the starry sky

378
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,039
and the deep sea.

379
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,640
An eternal night,

380
00:22:01,839 --> 00:22:04,680
without thought or dreams,

381
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,319
awaited her.

382
00:22:07,359 --> 00:22:08,279
Who are you?

383
00:22:08,839 --> 00:22:10,319
(She has no soul,)

384
00:22:10,599 --> 00:22:13,759
(and now could never win one.)

385
00:22:13,963 --> 00:22:14,470
Who's there?

386
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:16,758
Who are you? I'm the Little Mermaid!

387
00:22:16,759 --> 00:22:17,399
Who are you?

388
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:19,000
Stop! Stop right now!

389
00:22:19,759 --> 00:22:21,759
Let go of me!

390
00:22:27,893 --> 00:22:29,013
What's going on?

391
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:30,920
Su Lin...

392
00:22:34,759 --> 00:22:35,399
(Stop!)

393
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,679
(Everyone, stop right now!)

394
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,759
- Ma Na!
- (I said stop!)

395
00:22:38,359 --> 00:22:39,079
What are you doing?

396
00:22:39,319 --> 00:22:40,039
Get off the stage!

397
00:22:40,319 --> 00:22:41,399
She's not from our school.

398
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,199
She's causing trouble.

399
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:43,399
I'm the Little Mermaid!

400
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,000
- I'm the Little Mermaid!
- Get off!

401
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:47,480
Let go! Let go!

402
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:48,920
Let go!

403
00:22:49,799 --> 00:22:51,000
I'm not here to cause trouble.

404
00:22:52,039 --> 00:22:53,519
I'm here to compete.

405
00:22:57,519 --> 00:22:58,519
That was amazing!

406
00:22:58,759 --> 00:22:59,440
Good.

407
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,279
Stop clapping!

408
00:23:04,599 --> 00:23:05,559
Everyone, stop clapping!

409
00:23:05,799 --> 00:23:08,480
Great.

410
00:23:09,279 --> 00:23:09,999
Stop clapping!

411
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,119
I said stop clapping!

412
00:23:15,119 --> 00:23:16,079
Thank you, everyone.

413
00:23:39,119 --> 00:23:39,879
You...

414
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,680
bring her back!

415
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:45,720
Students,

416
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,519
we've had an unexpected incident.

417
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:48,558
The contest is paused.

418
00:23:48,559 --> 00:23:49,640
Please take a short break.

419
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,561
Stop clapping.

420
00:23:52,562 --> 00:23:57,920
♪ Lost eyes search the shadows ♪

421
00:23:58,815 --> 00:24:05,240
♪ So many stories hide in life's corners ♪

422
00:24:06,076 --> 00:24:11,323
♪ I remember every joy and sorrow ♪

423
00:24:11,429 --> 00:24:14,909
♪ Till a dazzling beam breaks through ♪

424
00:24:15,003 --> 00:24:16,558
♪ I know that light is salvation ♪

425
00:24:16,559 --> 00:24:17,079
Come with me.

426
00:24:18,223 --> 00:24:21,998
♪ The torn night declares an end ♪

427
00:24:21,999 --> 00:24:25,978
♪ And loneliness fades into nothing ♪

428
00:24:25,979 --> 00:24:31,943
♪ I'll fight free of the darkness ♪

429
00:24:32,030 --> 00:24:35,685
♪ And break the chains of fate ♪

430
00:24:35,686 --> 00:24:39,884
♪ Let me touch the blue sky above ♪

431
00:24:40,159 --> 00:24:45,879
♪ That light suddenly falls ♪

432
00:24:46,192 --> 00:24:51,586
♪ Saving all my broken pieces ♪

433
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:55,799
Go. Now!

434
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:57,118
Go!

435
00:24:57,119 --> 00:24:57,879
What about you?

436
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:58,680
Forget me. Just go!

437
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,799
Go!

438
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:04,059
Go!

439
00:25:04,060 --> 00:25:07,621
♪ The torn night declares an end ♪

440
00:25:07,622 --> 00:25:11,738
♪ And loneliness fades into nothing ♪

441
00:25:11,739 --> 00:25:17,949
♪ I'll fight free of the darkness ♪

442
00:25:17,950 --> 00:25:21,672
♪ And break the chains of fate ♪

443
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:22,440
(Go!)

444
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,160
(Run!)

445
00:25:25,923 --> 00:25:31,950
♪ That light suddenly falls ♪

446
00:25:32,050 --> 00:25:38,608
♪ Saving all my broken pieces ♪

447
00:25:42,844 --> 00:25:49,317
♪ It saves me ♪

448
00:25:49,537 --> 00:25:52,304
(Chaobei Vocational High School)

449
00:25:57,240 --> 00:25:58,358
How many times have I said it?

450
00:25:58,359 --> 00:25:59,680
Discipline!

451
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:01,880
Do you ever listen?

452
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:03,199
Something happened,

453
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:05,079
and somehow it's all on me.

454
00:26:05,839 --> 00:26:06,960
Go write a reflection.

455
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:08,960
Mom.

456
00:26:13,599 --> 00:26:15,559
You're Jiang Ting's mom, right?

457
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:18,558
Today, someone disrupted

458
00:26:18,559 --> 00:26:20,200
our school's recitation contest.

459
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,839
Your daughter let her get away.

460
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:24,719
First, I want to know

461
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:25,960
what exactly happened.

462
00:26:26,799 --> 00:26:27,400
Second,

463
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,719
that was a breach of discipline.

464
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:30,720
It must be dealt with.

465
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:32,720
As her parent, you owe us an explanation.

466
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:34,960
Mom.

467
00:26:41,319 --> 00:26:42,319
What's going on?

468
00:26:42,839 --> 00:26:43,519
It's her.

469
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:45,399
She's back.

470
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:46,119
Who?

471
00:26:46,519 --> 00:26:47,200
Su Lin.

472
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:49,839
Su Lin?

473
00:27:00,079 --> 00:27:01,599
What are you two doing?

474
00:27:05,559 --> 00:27:06,799
I knew what she was trying to do.

475
00:27:07,119 --> 00:27:07,839
So I helped her.

476
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:11,039
I'm talking to you!

477
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,440
Ma'am,

478
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,518
do you know how important

479
00:27:13,519 --> 00:27:15,000
this contest is to our school?

480
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:17,199
Because of what your daughter did,

481
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,318
I don't even know

482
00:27:18,319 --> 00:27:19,879
how to explain this to my superiors.

483
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:21,318
Can you understand my position?

484
00:27:21,319 --> 00:27:22,279
I do.

485
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:24,559
Please calm down and hear me out.

486
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:25,440
Principal Dong,

487
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,279
why was someone able to disrupt

488
00:27:28,839 --> 00:27:30,160
a contest at your school?

489
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,920
Ask security, the teachers, or police.

490
00:27:32,279 --> 00:27:33,920
Find out what really happened.

491
00:27:34,079 --> 00:27:35,439
I already did.

492
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:37,838
Your daughter let that person go.

493
00:27:37,839 --> 00:27:38,559
Do you understand?

494
00:27:38,759 --> 00:27:39,518
You don't believe me?

495
00:27:39,519 --> 00:27:41,079
I do. I absolutely do.

496
00:27:41,279 --> 00:27:42,359
I know my daughter.

497
00:27:42,759 --> 00:27:44,200
She isn't reckless,

498
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:45,920
and she wouldn't knowingly
help someone bad.

499
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:47,680
There has to be a reason.

500
00:27:48,039 --> 00:27:48,880
I believe her.

501
00:27:49,559 --> 00:27:51,079
And I want the truth too.

502
00:27:51,279 --> 00:27:52,199
so that my daughter

503
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,640
won't be blamed
for something she didn't do.

504
00:27:53,799 --> 00:27:55,999
What kind of attitude is this?

505
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:57,399
What do school rules

506
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,199
mean to you people?

507
00:27:58,200 --> 00:27:59,839
Now you're questioning me?

508
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:00,879
- Find out why.
- Let's go.

509
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:01,959
Find out what really happened.

510
00:28:01,960 --> 00:28:02,680
I'm sorry.

511
00:28:02,839 --> 00:28:04,039
I raised my voice just now.

512
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,598
Can we stick to the facts?

513
00:28:05,599 --> 00:28:06,318
That attitude...

514
00:28:06,319 --> 00:28:07,759
Like student, like parent.

515
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:09,680
Like mother, like daughter.

516
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:11,758
What kind of parent acts like this?

517
00:28:11,759 --> 00:28:12,359
Stop!

518
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:13,839
Stop!

519
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,720
Are you with them?

520
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:19,199
You all teamed up

521
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:20,078
to threaten and scare me.

522
00:28:20,079 --> 00:28:21,519
You even locked me in a bathroom today!

523
00:28:22,359 --> 00:28:23,798
I don't know what you're talking about.

524
00:28:23,799 --> 00:28:25,160
You're not leaving until you explain.

525
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,400
Wait. Who are you?

526
00:28:26,599 --> 00:28:27,519
Calm down.

527
00:28:29,319 --> 00:28:30,119
She's Ma Na.

528
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:43,119
So you're Ma Na.

529
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:46,440
Look me in the eye.

530
00:28:49,279 --> 00:28:51,319
If you ever bully Jiang Ting again,

531
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,319
I won't let you off.

532
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,519
Got it?

533
00:28:56,119 --> 00:28:56,599
Go.

534
00:28:58,960 --> 00:28:59,440
Ma Na.

535
00:29:01,519 --> 00:29:02,399
That woman is impossible.

536
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,759
Mr. Dong, you have to help me.

537
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,399
They threatened me. They scared me.

538
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:06,758
They all said Su Lin was dead.

539
00:29:06,759 --> 00:29:08,038
They even tricked me
into giving them money.

540
00:29:08,039 --> 00:29:09,318
What do you mean Su Lin is dead?

541
00:29:09,319 --> 00:29:10,038
What are you saying?

542
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:11,640
- They gave me a box...
- Sir.

543
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:13,559
Yes?

544
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:16,799
The bureau leadership

545
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,640
heard about today's incident.

546
00:29:18,759 --> 00:29:19,759
They want to see you.

547
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:20,758
Sir,

548
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,078
you have to look into this.

549
00:29:22,079 --> 00:29:23,439
This can't just be ignored.

550
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:24,479
If my dad finds out,

551
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:24,999
he'll...

552
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:26,519
What if your dad finds out?

553
00:29:26,799 --> 00:29:28,160
Have we treated you badly?

554
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:29,920
Haven't we helped you?

555
00:29:30,079 --> 00:29:31,079
How much work did you put

556
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:32,119
into this contest?

557
00:29:32,279 --> 00:29:33,200
Do you even value it?

558
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:36,479
I have to report to my superiors now.

559
00:29:36,480 --> 00:29:37,319
Do you understand?

560
00:29:41,119 --> 00:29:41,920
You two carry on.

561
00:30:04,850 --> 00:30:11,203
(Waiting Room)

562
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:26,799
(The Story King)
Wait here.

563
00:30:27,599 --> 00:30:28,400
Hold your bag.

564
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:30,078
There's a little mermaid here.

565
00:30:30,079 --> 00:30:30,559
Picture.

566
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:35,680
Picture.

567
00:30:36,799 --> 00:30:37,359
Picture.

568
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:39,559
Picture.

569
00:30:41,519 --> 00:30:42,079
Picture.

570
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:46,720
Picture.

571
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:50,440
Xiaolan...

572
00:30:50,759 --> 00:30:52,160
Xiaolan's picture.

573
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:54,920
X-X-Xiaolan's picture.

574
00:30:55,279 --> 00:30:56,279
Xiaolan's picture.

575
00:30:56,703 --> 00:30:57,679
There.

576
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:58,640
Xiaolan's picture.

577
00:30:59,799 --> 00:31:00,880
Xiaolan's picture.

578
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:05,480
Xiaolan's picture.

579
00:31:08,119 --> 00:31:10,000
X-Xiaolan's picture.

580
00:31:10,799 --> 00:31:11,799
Xiaolan's picture.

581
00:31:13,039 --> 00:31:14,039
Xiaolan's picture.

582
00:32:04,039 --> 00:32:04,880
What's your name?

583
00:32:05,519 --> 00:32:06,160
